## 21. Project abstract

ExamFlow – Online Examination Management System

ExamFlow is a web-based online examination management platform developed to simplify and modernize the examination process in educational institutions. The system provides separate interfaces for administrators and students, allowing administrators to manage subjects, create examinations, configure examination schedules and durations, and enter questions in multiple formats, including multiple-choice, descriptive, and programming questions.

The platform provides randomized question presentation, server-controlled examination timing, automatic answer saving, full-screen monitoring, and tab-switch detection. Programming questions are evaluated through an isolated code execution environment using predefined test cases. Multiple-choice questions are automatically evaluated, while descriptive answers can be manually assessed by administrators. The system generates examination results and publishes them to students after evaluation.

The primary objective of ExamFlow is to provide a reliable, scalable, secure, and user-friendly digital examination environment that reduces manual examination management and supports different assessment methods through a single platform.

